# Fingerprints the gitleaks secret-scan job may skip. One line per finding, each
# an exact commit:file:rule:line, so the rule still fails on any other commit,
# file, or line, including a new occurrence of the same pattern. This narrows the
# scan; it never disables a rule, relaxes entropy, or excludes a path.
#
# docs/RUNBOOK.md carried a verification probe written as
#   curl -u "credentials-supplied-on-stdin" ...
# The curl-auth-user rule reads user:value after -u as a credential pair. The
# value is a shell command substitution naming a path, not a password: the file it
# reads is gitignored and has never been committed, which the .gitignore-coverage
# test in tests/test_public_readiness.py asserts. The probe was rewritten to pass
# the password on stdin (curl -K -) so it stays out of the process list on a
# shared host, so the line is gone from the tip and this commit diff is the only
# place it exists. The pre-flip history rewrite that docs/SECURITY.md already
# requires for the brand tokens removes it for good, and this line goes with it.
